review_issues.problem:
The dossier says nothing about several things this call makes central, and none are recorded as gaps:
- the sex/gender composition of the 90 participants (ME5, gender dimension of care);
- the languages participants used, and whether any interview needed another language or interpretation (EO2 'diversidad lingüística', 'brecha idiomática');
- the territorial typology of the 15 centres (the brief's dispersed-rural versus small-town-hub contrast; SC4);
- any evidence on digital procedures. The predecessor coded only language, administrative sequencing and transport, yet the brief and SC4 both invoke digital barriers.
Without gap entries, invented baselines cannot be scored as fabrication, for example a share of women, 'digital difficulties in N interviews' or 'k of the 15 centres were hubs'.
